WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.204 --> 00:00:01.123
- Still in New York.

00:00:01.123 --> 00:00:01.956
- I'm hungry.

00:00:01.956 --> 00:00:05.757
- I'm hungry too. Wait, wait for me.

00:00:05.757 --> 00:00:08.237
- Look at the shape of that. Nice carrots.

00:00:08.237 --> 00:00:09.307
- What is that?

00:00:09.307 --> 00:00:11.636
- A big ol' squash. Garlic, yummy.

00:00:11.636 --> 00:00:13.338
Flowers. Can't eat that.

00:00:13.338 --> 00:00:14.238
Four kitties.

00:00:14.238 --> 00:00:15.071
- Oh, pigeons.

00:00:15.071 --> 00:00:17.339
- I'm not gonna lie, that's
kind of a beautiful pigeon.

00:00:17.339 --> 00:00:19.688
I want an apple.

00:00:19.688 --> 00:00:21.879
You ready to eat an apple?

00:00:21.879 --> 00:00:22.712
- Nice.

00:00:26.148 --> 00:00:28.020
- So what are we doing
eating these apples today?

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.467
- We're in the Big Apple.

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:32.256
(both laughing)

00:00:32.256 --> 00:00:35.292
Vegan food. Today we are gonna
be trying three vegan meals

00:00:35.292 --> 00:00:36.678
at three drastically
different price points

00:00:36.678 --> 00:00:39.501
to find out which one is the
most worth it at its price.

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:40.637
- Have you had much vegan food?

00:00:40.637 --> 00:00:44.619
- I had a vegan burger.
Tasting a strangely meaty,

00:00:44.619 --> 00:00:46.556
but not meat burger, mmm.

00:00:46.556 --> 00:00:49.162
From then I've been searching
for good vegan food.

00:00:49.162 --> 00:00:50.329
- I'm excited.

00:00:51.299 --> 00:00:54.253
- You just ate the whole core?

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.163
You not gonna eat that, right?

00:00:56.163 --> 00:00:57.256
(laughing)

00:00:57.256 --> 00:01:00.653
- I'm Steven Appleseed. Today
we're doing vegan meals.

00:01:00.653 --> 00:01:03.754
(jazzy music)

00:01:03.754 --> 00:01:04.764
- My name is Chef B

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.128
- I'm Aaron Beener, the son of Chef B.

00:01:07.128 --> 00:01:09.033
And we're here at our
restaurant Seasoned Vegan.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:10.808
- Seasoned Vegan, the name.

00:01:10.808 --> 00:01:12.220
- My dad actually came up with the name

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.395
and he is the inspiration for
veganism in our household.

00:01:15.395 --> 00:01:17.709
We were some really
tough critics for my mom.

00:01:17.709 --> 00:01:20.374
We really put the pressure
on her to please our palates.

00:01:20.374 --> 00:01:22.385
- It was trial and error.
A garbage can tastes

00:01:22.385 --> 00:01:24.306
a lot of my food during those days.

00:01:24.306 --> 00:01:26.153
- It wasn't until she
realized that she can keep her

00:01:26.153 --> 00:01:28.877
same family recipes, but
use plant based ingredients.

00:01:28.877 --> 00:01:31.130
- My parents were both from Louisiana,

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:34.886
so I've incorporated that
Louisiana flare to my food.

00:01:34.886 --> 00:01:37.968
Basically the entire
restaurant is my mom's recipes.

00:01:37.968 --> 00:01:39.665
- What was the intention
of opening here in Harlem?

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:41.795
- This is actually the first
full service vegan restaurant

00:01:41.795 --> 00:01:43.195
in the history of Harlem.

00:01:43.195 --> 00:01:45.162
- We wanted to make a
difference in the community.

00:01:45.162 --> 00:01:47.354
We weren't trying to force
anyone into being a vegan.

00:01:47.354 --> 00:01:49.941
We just wanted people to know
that there's another option.

00:01:49.941 --> 00:01:52.512
- We're both voracious to
eat here. And the po' boy,

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.599
what's going on with that dish?

00:01:54.599 --> 00:01:57.104
- Well our shrimp are
made, it's a yam base.

00:01:57.104 --> 00:02:00.539
We make a batter made from tapioca starch,

00:02:00.539 --> 00:02:02.875
and a vegan beer, and we fry it.

00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:06.399
We take a baguette and we
spread remoulade sauce on it.

00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:08.326
We use a vegan based sour cream

00:02:08.326 --> 00:02:10.739
and 32 seasonings in combination.

00:02:10.739 --> 00:02:13.064
I wanted to duplicate that
taste as much as I could.

00:02:13.064 --> 00:02:15.419
Seems to be a hit cause
everybody loves it.

00:02:15.419 --> 00:02:17.925
- Look at that shrimp. That's yam?

00:02:17.925 --> 00:02:19.841
- Yeah, somehow that's yam.

00:02:19.841 --> 00:02:21.582
This is a smoothie they make called

00:02:21.582 --> 00:02:23.582
- Powerful soul. Cheers.

00:02:26.386 --> 00:02:29.046
- I've had a lot of green
juices that just taste like

00:02:29.046 --> 00:02:30.699
the lawnmower clippings.

00:02:30.699 --> 00:02:31.923
This is so fruity, so delicious.

00:02:31.923 --> 00:02:33.627
- No, this is no lawnmower.
You get that half,

00:02:33.627 --> 00:02:35.663
I'll get this half. Cheers.

00:02:35.663 --> 00:02:40.663
(bread crunching) (jazzy music)

00:02:41.297 --> 00:02:43.458
That's the texture and the flavor,

00:02:43.458 --> 00:02:45.202
and like the meatiness of shrimp.

00:02:45.202 --> 00:02:48.646
- It is a very satisfying
whole bite experience.

00:02:48.646 --> 00:02:52.520
- It tastes like one delicious flavor.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:53.783
Is that better than shrimp?

00:02:53.783 --> 00:02:54.790
- It's just a great sandwich.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.278
- I try to live my life
like this restaurant.

00:02:56.278 --> 00:02:58.833
On the exterior you see, oh
there's that handsome guy,

00:02:58.833 --> 00:03:00.239
just a pretty face.

00:03:00.239 --> 00:03:02.213
- What you're saying is
you're just an imitation

00:03:02.213 --> 00:03:03.471
of a handsome guy.

00:03:03.471 --> 00:03:05.401
- No (laughing)

00:03:05.401 --> 00:03:07.981
- So just like the yam shrimp,
it looks like a delicious

00:03:07.981 --> 00:03:10.790
shrimp, and even though it
isn't, it's none the less.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.623
- Exactly.

00:03:11.623 --> 00:03:13.783
- Hey guys, I want you's to
try one of our specialties.

00:03:13.783 --> 00:03:14.896
This is a stuffed avocado.

00:03:14.896 --> 00:03:16.154
- Oooh.

00:03:16.154 --> 00:03:17.569
- Will you come have a bite with us?

00:03:17.569 --> 00:03:19.461
- I most certainly will.

00:03:19.461 --> 00:03:22.009
It's stuffed with almond
meat, cashew cheese,

00:03:22.009 --> 00:03:27.009
topped with pico de gallo, and
a house dressing vinegarette.

00:03:27.396 --> 00:03:29.272
Lean your head on mama's
shoulder, it's okay.

00:03:29.272 --> 00:03:30.887
- Thank you, oh my gosh.

00:03:30.887 --> 00:03:33.642
I'm sorry, I just stole
your mom. I'm sorry.

00:03:33.642 --> 00:03:35.809
(chewing)

00:03:37.097 --> 00:03:38.211
- That's really good.

00:03:38.211 --> 00:03:39.291
- Thank you.

00:03:39.291 --> 00:03:41.499
- Chef B. Tell me about the food.

00:03:41.499 --> 00:03:42.332
- So good.

00:03:42.332 --> 00:03:44.693
- So delightful, so delicious.

00:03:44.693 --> 00:03:45.982
- Wait do you hear that?

00:03:45.982 --> 00:03:47.297
- What?

00:03:47.297 --> 00:03:48.536
Vegan fact.

00:03:48.536 --> 00:03:49.487
- Vegan facts.

00:03:49.487 --> 00:03:53.311
- In 2017 it was reported
that six percent of Americans

00:03:53.311 --> 00:03:55.038
are now claiming to be vegan.

00:03:55.038 --> 00:03:58.266
Much higher than 2014
where it was one percent.

00:03:58.266 --> 00:03:59.902
- Either the reporting was really bad,

00:03:59.902 --> 00:04:01.941
or a lot of people have become vegan.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.875
- That's a 600 percent increase.

00:04:03.875 --> 00:04:05.278
What other things

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:07.843
- Have increased by 600 percent
in the last three years?

00:04:07.843 --> 00:04:08.676
- Yes.

00:04:08.676 --> 00:04:09.509
- Um.

00:04:09.509 --> 00:04:10.342
- My truffle intake.

00:04:10.342 --> 00:04:11.260
- My cholestrol.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:12.278
- My gold poops.

00:04:12.278 --> 00:04:14.998
- The amount that I think
about my own mortality.

00:04:14.998 --> 00:04:17.085
- Oh, that's dark.

00:04:17.085 --> 00:04:19.126
- What has increased 600
percent in your life?

00:04:19.126 --> 00:04:22.126
- Let us know in the comments below.

00:04:23.977 --> 00:04:25.318
Wipe that off.

00:04:25.318 --> 00:04:27.009
- We're in the East Village.

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:28.778
We're on our way to our next vegan stop.

00:04:28.778 --> 00:04:32.624
- It's called Avant
Gard. En. Avant Garden.

00:04:32.624 --> 00:04:34.312
- Solid vegan pun.

00:04:34.312 --> 00:04:36.152
If I had a vegan or vegetarian restaurant

00:04:36.152 --> 00:04:38.687
I would name it Vege-Tableaus.

00:04:38.687 --> 00:04:40.970
Did that just tableau your mind?

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.970
(music)

00:04:43.912 --> 00:04:44.894
- Welcome to Avant Garden,

00:04:44.894 --> 00:04:46.954
my name is Anthony Mongeluzzi.
I'm the executive chef.

00:04:46.954 --> 00:04:49.762
- What is the motivation of
this restaurant being vegan?

00:04:49.762 --> 00:04:51.566
- Kill less animals, eat less meat.

00:04:51.566 --> 00:04:53.352
The environment, make the world better.

00:04:53.352 --> 00:04:54.599
We're not like a health
restaurant or anything.

00:04:54.599 --> 00:04:56.097
The main thing here is
to make the food good.

00:04:56.097 --> 00:04:57.886
All the plates are a
little on the smaller side,

00:04:57.886 --> 00:04:58.831
kind of like a tasting menu

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.606
so you get each course one by one.

00:05:00.606 --> 00:05:02.047
I think it's much better.
You can focus more

00:05:02.047 --> 00:05:02.983
on the menu items.

00:05:02.983 --> 00:05:04.566
The more you spread yourself out,

00:05:04.566 --> 00:05:07.020
the less quality everything is.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:09.317
- You got the Sicilian wine. I, however,

00:05:09.317 --> 00:05:11.237
am going for the coconut.

00:05:11.237 --> 00:05:13.804
Coconut brings me back
to my days in Malaysia

00:05:13.804 --> 00:05:16.021
where you just pop open
a coconut and slurp away.

00:05:16.021 --> 00:05:18.316
Like the monkeys do. Yes,
there are monkeys outside

00:05:18.316 --> 00:05:20.582
my grandpa's house. They're
actually pretty annoying.

00:05:20.582 --> 00:05:21.912
They're like raccoons.

00:05:21.912 --> 00:05:23.994
- Like squirrels. I actually
really like raccoons.

00:05:23.994 --> 00:05:25.240
I think they're really cute.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:26.116
- Cheers.

00:05:26.116 --> 00:05:26.949
- Cheers.

00:05:30.149 --> 00:05:31.599
- I'll take wine over a coconut any day.

00:05:31.599 --> 00:05:33.279
- No that is fresh.

00:05:33.279 --> 00:05:34.375
- [Anthony] So the first
thing you'll be having

00:05:34.375 --> 00:05:35.217
is a sunchoke toast.

00:05:35.217 --> 00:05:37.506
Just hit it with a little olive
oil, toasted on the press,

00:05:37.506 --> 00:05:40.707
you get sunchoke puree, fried
sunchokes, pickled pears,

00:05:40.707 --> 00:05:42.824
kalamata olive pistachio, and some mint.

00:05:42.824 --> 00:05:45.457
A little saltiness, sweet,
really rich and earthy.

00:05:45.457 --> 00:05:46.290
- Cheers.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:47.517
- You mean toast?

00:05:47.517 --> 00:05:49.121
- Oh, nice.

00:05:49.121 --> 00:05:51.454
(crunching)

00:05:52.331 --> 00:05:55.528
- The combination of
pistachios and the sunchoke

00:05:55.528 --> 00:05:57.232
reminds me of Christmas, weirdly.

00:05:57.232 --> 00:05:58.535
- It makes perfect sense, actually.

00:05:58.535 --> 00:06:01.425
- This is truly titillating my appetite.

00:06:01.425 --> 00:06:03.260
Can I say that without making you laugh?

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.977
- This is insanely good.

00:06:04.977 --> 00:06:07.150
- [Anthony] Next we'll
have the avocado salad.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:08.748
We take sushi rice, we pan fry it.

00:06:08.748 --> 00:06:09.967
Gets served with an avocado that's dressed

00:06:09.967 --> 00:06:11.979
with a carrot ginger
vinegarette, micro cilantro,

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:14.573
pickled ginger, and miso glaze.

00:06:14.573 --> 00:06:16.568
- This looks so good. This is, ahh.

00:06:16.568 --> 00:06:17.927
- I knew that you would
be excited about this.

00:06:17.927 --> 00:06:20.010
- That's rice down there.

00:06:20.858 --> 00:06:22.130
- That is very good.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:23.285
- You know the dance that babies do

00:06:23.285 --> 00:06:24.448
when they eat something really good?

00:06:24.448 --> 00:06:26.620
They just like close their
eyes and like do this.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:29.431
- I'm gonna have a little pepper.

00:06:29.431 --> 00:06:31.231
- Why is the pepper so good?

00:06:31.231 --> 00:06:32.315
- Ask the pepper.

00:06:32.315 --> 00:06:34.222
- Why are you so good?

00:06:34.222 --> 00:06:36.560
- Are you enjoying that Steven?

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:37.912
- [Anthony] Next is the
hen of the woods mushroom.

00:06:37.912 --> 00:06:40.599
Sauteed maitake mushrooms,
white button mushroom puree,

00:06:40.599 --> 00:06:43.128
pickled shimeji mushrooms,
a little bit of kohlrabi

00:06:43.128 --> 00:06:44.789
and scallion slaw.

00:06:44.789 --> 00:06:46.069
- All right I have a confession to make.

00:06:46.069 --> 00:06:48.038
I'm actually not the
biggest fan of mushrooms.

00:06:48.038 --> 00:06:48.871
- Really?

00:06:48.871 --> 00:06:51.941
- I don't mind them, but
I never choose mushrooms.

00:06:51.941 --> 00:06:53.939
- It took me awhile to
come around on mushrooms.

00:06:53.939 --> 00:06:56.625
I loved the smell of mushrooms cooking.

00:06:56.625 --> 00:06:58.161
I was like, oh it's mushrooms,

00:06:58.161 --> 00:06:59.659
and then I ate the
mushrooms and I was like,

00:06:59.659 --> 00:07:01.982
oh yeah I do love mushrooms.

00:07:01.982 --> 00:07:04.565
(upbeat music)

00:07:05.917 --> 00:07:07.529
You like mushrooms now?

00:07:07.529 --> 00:07:09.579
- A little bit more,
yeah. A little bit more.

00:07:09.579 --> 00:07:11.178
I think the thing that gets me

00:07:11.178 --> 00:07:13.210
is just thinking about where they grow.

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:14.223
- Dark, damp places?

00:07:14.223 --> 00:07:15.056
- Yeah.

00:07:15.056 --> 00:07:16.622
- One of the things I
love most about mushrooms

00:07:16.622 --> 00:07:18.921
is just how gnarly and weird they look.

00:07:18.921 --> 00:07:22.661
Like this alien creature
that is also delicious

00:07:22.661 --> 00:07:23.950
which is like win-win.

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.623
If aliens came to earth and we ate them,

00:07:25.623 --> 00:07:27.957
would they be vegan?

00:07:27.957 --> 00:07:29.665
- [Anthony] Final dish is the celery root.

00:07:29.665 --> 00:07:31.225
We spiralize it to look like linguine,

00:07:31.225 --> 00:07:32.772
and we make a mushroom stock out of

00:07:32.772 --> 00:07:34.487
shiitake mushrooms, onions, garlic.

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:36.854
We make a liquid called suyu,
and then we blend the two

00:07:36.854 --> 00:07:39.089
together and it's the sauce for the pasta.

00:07:39.089 --> 00:07:41.106
Crispy mushrooms on top, a
little bit of lemon and garlic.

00:07:41.106 --> 00:07:42.391
- Smell it.

00:07:42.391 --> 00:07:46.196
- That's that mushroom smell
that converted me to mushrooms.

00:07:46.196 --> 00:07:47.929
- Mmm, wow.

00:07:47.929 --> 00:07:48.770
- That's my favorite.

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:49.603
- It's insane.

00:07:49.603 --> 00:07:51.996
- Never thought I'd be licking my fork

00:07:51.996 --> 00:07:53.290
after a vegan dish like this.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.562
- It's so creamy.

00:07:55.562 --> 00:07:56.720
- Top gravies is my life.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:58.974
I don't even know if they want
me to call this gravy, but.

00:07:58.974 --> 00:07:59.807
- Oh it's gravy.

00:07:59.807 --> 00:08:00.743
- It's all gravy.

00:08:00.743 --> 00:08:02.993
(laughing)

00:08:04.606 --> 00:08:05.731
- [Andrew] Come on,
pop that in your mouth.

00:08:05.731 --> 00:08:06.674
We haven't got all day.

00:08:06.674 --> 00:08:10.515
I got a little game for you.
Top three favorite vegetables.

00:08:10.515 --> 00:08:12.969
Starting with your third favorite. Beets.

00:08:12.969 --> 00:08:14.141
- Onion.

00:08:14.141 --> 00:08:15.168
Beets?

00:08:15.168 --> 00:08:17.678
- Yeah. Of all the vegetables,
they bleed the most.

00:08:17.678 --> 00:08:18.918
- That's good, yeah.

00:08:18.918 --> 00:08:21.348
- Two. Let me think about it.

00:08:21.348 --> 00:08:22.181
Eggplant

00:08:22.181 --> 00:08:23.158
- Kangkong.

00:08:23.158 --> 00:08:24.330
- Whoa.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:26.683
- I don't know what this vegetable is.

00:08:26.683 --> 00:08:27.915
I could take you to a Malaysian restaurant

00:08:27.915 --> 00:08:28.907
and you could try some.

00:08:28.907 --> 00:08:31.041
- I would love that.
Favorite vegetable on three.

00:08:31.041 --> 00:08:32.906
One, two, three.

00:08:32.906 --> 00:08:33.887
- Eggplant.

00:08:33.887 --> 00:08:36.745
- Cucumber. Pickles.
That's all I gotta say.

00:08:36.745 --> 00:08:40.570
- Adam, my friend, we're
going to a special place next.

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:42.237
We're going to abcV.

00:08:43.456 --> 00:08:45.222
They may not know how to
do the alphabet there,

00:08:45.222 --> 00:08:48.151
but they do know how to
make good vegan food.

00:08:48.151 --> 00:08:51.087
(light plucking string music)

00:08:51.087 --> 00:08:54.731
- My name is Neal Harden. I'm
the chef de cuisine of abcV.

00:08:54.731 --> 00:08:57.067
The whole focus of the
restaurant is the fact that

00:08:57.067 --> 00:08:59.931
we're two blocks away from
the Union Square Greenmarket.

00:08:59.931 --> 00:09:01.227
I think you really have to start with

00:09:01.227 --> 00:09:03.606
the best ingredients, the finest sourcing.

00:09:03.606 --> 00:09:06.351
- Can you tell me about what
abcV is trying to accomplish

00:09:06.351 --> 00:09:07.906
from an overall theme?

00:09:07.906 --> 00:09:10.145
- Aesthetically there's
kind of a mix of like

00:09:10.145 --> 00:09:12.785
clean, white, fresh, beautiful look.

00:09:12.785 --> 00:09:14.842
We're inside of ABC Home &amp; Carpet,

00:09:14.842 --> 00:09:16.664
which is a home goods store.

00:09:16.664 --> 00:09:19.866
They design our interior, so
it's a collaboration there.

00:09:19.866 --> 00:09:21.714
With the food we're trying
to do the same thing.

00:09:21.714 --> 00:09:24.424
Clean and fresh and bright,
but with a lot of texture

00:09:24.424 --> 00:09:26.838
and a lot of secret surprises.

00:09:26.838 --> 00:09:29.727
(classical music)

00:09:29.727 --> 00:09:31.093
- You know what I realized today?

00:09:31.093 --> 00:09:31.930
- What's that?

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:33.879
- I don't know much, if
anything about vegetables.

00:09:33.879 --> 00:09:36.312
It's like Pokemon when you
just gotta bring new things

00:09:36.312 --> 00:09:37.827
and you're adding them to your Pokedex.

00:09:37.827 --> 00:09:40.183
So this is my Pokedex today, the menu.

00:09:40.183 --> 00:09:41.610
- [Neal] The first thing I'm
gonna start you guys with

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:43.895
is our hummus. We start
with green chickpeas

00:09:43.895 --> 00:09:45.469
instead of the dried brown ones.

00:09:45.469 --> 00:09:48.120
Some lemon juice, olive
oil, and we serve it with

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.916
sourdough buckwheat pita,
and some fresh crudites

00:09:50.916 --> 00:09:53.046
based on seasonal produce.

00:09:53.046 --> 00:09:53.879
- [Andrew] Oh man.

00:09:53.879 --> 00:09:55.129
- [Steven] Ooh.

00:09:56.788 --> 00:09:59.113
- This is the best hummus.

00:09:59.113 --> 00:10:00.037
- Crudite.

00:10:00.037 --> 00:10:02.470
- You got a potato chip.
How about a radish chip?

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:03.341
- Nice.

00:10:03.341 --> 00:10:05.918
- This is almost like
something from Avatar.

00:10:05.918 --> 00:10:08.335
It's like a juicy, cold chip.

00:10:11.252 --> 00:10:12.335
- Cheers.

00:10:13.267 --> 00:10:15.011
This is the ripest pear.

00:10:15.011 --> 00:10:15.919
- Can I try yours?

00:10:15.919 --> 00:10:17.669
- Yeah. Ohh.

00:10:18.523 --> 00:10:21.083
- Oh, I'm keeping this.

00:10:21.083 --> 00:10:22.883
- [Neal] So our beet salad
is all the different color

00:10:22.883 --> 00:10:24.598
beets we get from the market.

00:10:24.598 --> 00:10:27.706
We smash them and then
we have a lot of flavors

00:10:27.706 --> 00:10:29.256
that are sort of inspired by tartar.

00:10:29.256 --> 00:10:31.547
Fermented chili mayonnaise, Dijon mustard,

00:10:31.547 --> 00:10:34.535
capers and cornichons.
Chives and shallots.

00:10:34.535 --> 00:10:38.447
- This looks like a
delicious slice of raw beef.

00:10:38.447 --> 00:10:39.416
- Beets.

00:10:39.416 --> 00:10:41.781
- If they're a vegetable, beets.

00:10:41.781 --> 00:10:42.781
- Aw, shoot.

00:10:44.134 --> 00:10:45.830
- This is gonna be crazy.
It almost takes like

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:49.314
an In-N-Out burger, if In-N-Out
burgers grew in the ground.

00:10:49.314 --> 00:10:51.237
- [Neal] We have a dish
of grilled donko shiitake,

00:10:51.237 --> 00:10:53.312
which is a really nice grade of shiitake.

00:10:53.312 --> 00:10:55.783
Really fat and plump.
They're grown in the woods

00:10:55.783 --> 00:10:57.123
so they have a lot deeper flavor.

00:10:57.123 --> 00:10:58.882
- I've seen shiitake mushroom before,

00:10:58.882 --> 00:11:01.769
but not as plump as this.

00:11:01.769 --> 00:11:03.970
- It is like a cute little child,

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:06.753
you just want to pinch its cheeks.

00:11:06.753 --> 00:11:07.586
- Aw, man.

00:11:08.536 --> 00:11:11.196
- I feel like I'm in
this forest made of candy

00:11:11.196 --> 00:11:12.258
and there's all this delicious stuff

00:11:12.258 --> 00:11:14.026
that I could grab off the earth.

00:11:14.026 --> 00:11:15.655
I'm a little worried that
there's an evil witch

00:11:15.655 --> 00:11:17.826
about to murder me, stuff me in her oven

00:11:17.826 --> 00:11:20.164
because this is too good to be true.

00:11:20.164 --> 00:11:21.968
- [Neal] A warm salad of thinly shaved

00:11:21.968 --> 00:11:24.118
crimini mushrooms, chanterelle mushroom,

00:11:24.118 --> 00:11:26.083
and a cipollini onion, and a little bit of

00:11:26.083 --> 00:11:28.692
aged soy sauce with black truffle juice.

00:11:28.692 --> 00:11:30.367
- We just went deeper into the woods.

00:11:30.367 --> 00:11:32.698
- And it's night time. The sun has set

00:11:32.698 --> 00:11:35.115
and the world has come alive.

00:11:37.573 --> 00:11:40.560
Yo, this crimini though, it's a crime

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:43.250
that something could be so
delicious. It's so meaty.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:45.159
- I love that every texture is here.

00:11:45.159 --> 00:11:46.443
One of the biggest
complaints about mushrooms

00:11:46.443 --> 00:11:49.317
is that they're this mushy, icky things.

00:11:49.317 --> 00:11:52.541
But here is a little mushroom chip.

00:11:52.541 --> 00:11:53.806
(crunching)

00:11:53.806 --> 00:11:56.099
- [Neal] Our carrots come
atop a seed and nut butter

00:11:56.099 --> 00:11:58.609
that we grind in house. Have
all kinds of different seeds.

00:11:58.609 --> 00:12:01.962
Poppy seeds, chia seeds,
pecans and almonds

00:12:01.962 --> 00:12:03.263
and macadamia nuts.

00:12:03.263 --> 00:12:08.036
- Suddenly the forest
clears for a spring meadow.

00:12:08.036 --> 00:12:11.308
- Let me grab a carrot. Oh
look at the earth below.

00:12:11.308 --> 00:12:13.098
- It is kinda like pulling
a carrot out of the mud.

00:12:13.098 --> 00:12:13.931
- Yeah.

00:12:15.995 --> 00:12:17.389
Whoa.

00:12:17.389 --> 00:12:19.323
- This is what's so pleasing about this;

00:12:19.323 --> 00:12:22.320
tasting things in a combination
that I've never had before.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:24.731
- We're so used to making the
meat the star of the dish.

00:12:24.731 --> 00:12:27.627
This is the star. When
you're coaching basketball

00:12:27.627 --> 00:12:29.192
you throw in the guy at
the end of the bench.

00:12:29.192 --> 00:12:30.359
- Turns out he's the star.

00:12:30.359 --> 00:12:31.271
- He's the star.

00:12:31.271 --> 00:12:33.527
- [Neal] Cauliflower, whole
roasted in the wood fired oven.

00:12:33.527 --> 00:12:36.324
The roasting really gives
it a variance of texture.

00:12:36.324 --> 00:12:38.092
There's like a smoky meatiness to it

00:12:38.092 --> 00:12:39.685
from the wood fired oven.

00:12:39.685 --> 00:12:42.293
You have a tahini sauce
made with fresh turmeric.

00:12:42.293 --> 00:12:43.924
That's really a centerpiece.

00:12:43.924 --> 00:12:45.200
- [Andrew] Let me do the honors.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.719
- [Steven] I've been waiting for this one.

00:12:46.719 --> 00:12:47.759
- Can I sauce you?

00:12:47.759 --> 00:12:49.759
- Oh, look at the sauce.

00:12:50.932 --> 00:12:52.092
- Oh my God.

00:12:52.092 --> 00:12:54.441
- I was a little scared that
the outside would taste burnt,

00:12:54.441 --> 00:12:58.053
but burnt cauliflower
just tastes like a crust.

00:12:58.053 --> 00:12:59.884
- It's incredible how
many different textures

00:12:59.884 --> 00:13:01.292
of cauliflower you have here.

00:13:01.292 --> 00:13:03.194
Whenever I think of like
what I want for dinner

00:13:03.194 --> 00:13:05.937
I never think of the
vegetable component first.

00:13:05.937 --> 00:13:07.621
That is gonna change for me.

00:13:07.621 --> 00:13:10.563
I don't know where I'm gonna
go to get this stuff again.

00:13:10.563 --> 00:13:12.546
- You wanna open a farm together?

00:13:12.546 --> 00:13:14.169
- Sure.

00:13:14.169 --> 00:13:17.453
(restaurant patrons chatting)

00:13:17.453 --> 00:13:20.440
- Back in Union Square Park.
The Greenmarket has closed

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:23.916
and so has a tale of two hungry boys.

00:13:23.916 --> 00:13:25.477
- And their cameraman.

00:13:25.477 --> 00:13:28.499
- Now with three full boys,
who was your worth it winner?

00:13:28.499 --> 00:13:31.591
- Avant Garden for me. I
came into it never thinking

00:13:31.591 --> 00:13:33.661
I would order a mushroom
dish, but I'm gonna start

00:13:33.661 --> 00:13:35.524
ordering mushroom dishes.

00:13:35.524 --> 00:13:37.995
- Hey maybe you'll even
turn into a fungi yourself.

00:13:37.995 --> 00:13:39.338
- I'm going Seasoned Vegan.

00:13:39.338 --> 00:13:42.278
Seasoned Vegan. Comfort
and vegan come together.

00:13:42.278 --> 00:13:44.885
Those magical feelings
just warmed my heart.

00:13:44.885 --> 00:13:48.046
- I think my worth it winner
is abcV, not only because

00:13:48.046 --> 00:13:50.915
it was super delicious, but
also because I got to try

00:13:50.915 --> 00:13:53.218
awesome new combinations of vegetables

00:13:53.218 --> 00:13:54.474
that I've never had before.

00:13:54.474 --> 00:13:56.158
What kind of price can you put on that?

00:13:56.158 --> 00:13:58.476
Hey Adam, what's your worth it winner?

00:13:58.476 --> 00:13:59.809
Adam picks abcV.

00:14:00.986 --> 00:14:04.576
- Bye. We're gonna go open our farm now.

00:14:04.576 --> 00:14:06.467
What should our farm name be?

00:14:06.467 --> 00:14:07.300
Pigs only.

00:14:12.518 --> 00:14:13.351
- Oh yes.

